\b ## Section B: Long Scenario Questions (50 Points)\b0\par
\par
\b Question 33: Cloud Networking and Routing (25 Points)\b0\par
\par
\b Scenario:\b0  You are designing a private cloud network in OpenStack. You have an internal network private-net (10.0.1.0/24) and need to connect it to the physical external-net so your VMs can access the internet.\par
\par
1.1. In OpenStack, which resource sits between the private network and the external network to handle traffic routing and NAT? [4 Points]\par
\par
1.2. Provide the sequence of CLI commands to:\par
a) Create a router named my-router. [2 Points]\par
b) Set the gateway of the router to the external-net. [3 Points]\par
\par
1.3. Connectivity: You now need to link your private-net subnet to this router. Provide the command to add the subnet private-subnet to the router my-router. [5 Points]\par
\par
1.4. Troubleshooting: A VM on the private-net is "ACTIVE" and has an internal IP, but cannot reach Google (8.8.8.8).\par
a) Name two common networking reasons why this might happen. [4 Points]\par
b) Which command on the VM would you use to see the path the packets are taking? [2 Points]\par
\par
1.5. Floating IPs:\par
a) Explain why a Floating IP is necessary for a VM on a private subnet to be reached from the internet. [3 Points]\par
b) Provide the command to associate a floating IP (e.g., 203.0.113.10) with a VM named web-vm. [2 Points]\par
\par
\b Answer:\b0\par
1.1. \b Router\b0 .\par
1.2. a) \f0\fs22 openstack router create my-router\f1\fs24 . b) \f0\fs22 openstack router set --external-gateway external-net my-router\f1\fs24\par
1.3. \f0\fs22 openstack router add subnet my-router private-subnet\f1\fs24\par
1.4. a) Router missing gateway; subnet not added to router interface. b) \f0\fs22 traceroute\f1\fs24 .\par
1.5. a) Private IPs aren't routable; FIP provides 1-to-1 NAT. b) \f0\fs22 openstack server add floating ip web-vm 203.0.113.10\f1\fs24\par
\par
\b Question 34: Advanced Automation and Cloud-Init (25 Points)\b0\par
\par
\b Scenario:\b0  You are automating the deployment of 50 web servers. Each server must be updated, have git installed, and have a specific folder created on its first boot.\par
\par
1.1. You are using Cloud-Init. Which mandatory "header" must be at the very top of your YAML configuration file? [4 Points]\par
\par
1.2. Provide the cloud-config YAML snippet to install the package git and ensure all existing packages are updated to their latest versions. [6 Points]\par
\par
1.3. You want to run a custom bash command to create a directory at /opt/app_data. Which Cloud-Init key is used for running arbitrary shell commands? Provide the snippet. [5 Points]\par
\par
1.4. Debugging: After launching a VM with User Data, the folder was not created.\par
a) Where is the primary Cloud-Init log file located on a Linux system? [3 Points]\par
b) Which file contains the "result"/output of the scripts that ran during boot? [2 Points]\par
\par
1.5. Metadata Service:\par
a) What is the "Magic IP" address used by cloud instances to request their specific User Data? [2 Points]\par
b) Provide the curl command a VM can run to see its own hostname from the metadata service. [3 Points]\par
\par
\b Answer:\b0\par
1.1. \f0\fs22 #cloud-config\f1\fs24\par
1.2. \f0\fs22 package_upgrade: true\par
packages: [git]\f1\fs24\par
1.3. \f0\fs22 runcmd\f1\fs24 . Snippet: \f0\fs22 runcmd: [ [ mkdir, -p, /opt/app_data ] ]\f1\fs24\par
1.4. a) \f0\fs22 /var/log/cloud-init.log\f1\fs24 . b) \f0\fs22 /var/log/cloud-init-output.log\f1\fs24\par
1.5. a) \b 169.254.169.254\b0 . b) \f0\fs22 curl http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/hostname\f1\fs24\par
